        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofkershawsc.gov/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Haile Gold Mine, located three miles from Kershaw, was once the largest single producer of gold in the Appalachian region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kershaw%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kershaw is home to several sites on the National Register of Historic Places, including the Kershaw Depot and Unity Baptist Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kershaw%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kershaw drains west to Lick Creek and east to the Little Lynches River within the Lynches River watershed.",
